{"name":"Piedmont","hex":"#c2cec5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Piedmont","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An administrative region in the north of Italy.","A geographic region and plateau of the eastern United States, between the Appalachian mountains and the coastal plain, extending from eastern Alabama to northern New Jersey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Piedmont"}],"entries":[{"title":"Piedmont","blocks":[{"text":"Piedmont is one of the 20 regions of Italy, located in the Northwest of the country. It borders the Liguria region to the south, the Lombardy and Emilia-Romagna regions to the east, and the Aosta Valley region to the northwest. Piedmont borders Switzerland to the north and France to the west."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Piedmont_in_Italy.svg/330px-Piedmont_in_Italy.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piedmont","wikidata":"Q1216"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Torino-portapalatina01.jpg/500px-Torino-portapalatina01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Torino-portapalatina01.jpg/500px-Torino-portapalatina01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Roman Palatine Towers in Turin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATorino-portapalatina01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Valentino_castle.jpg/500px-Valentino_castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Valentino_castle.jpg/1280px-Valentino_castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/